  "body": "What happens: in a setup whose part alignment is not \"As modelled\", Generate refuses some operation kinds. The maintainer reported this message on 2026-11-16, \"on different operations\":\n\n```\ngenerate failed: could not generate the toolpath: 2D Offset1: invalid machining parameters: setup 'Setup1' holds the part turned (part alignment) - 2D Offset is not supported yet in an aligned setup (Face, 2D Contour, 2D Pocket, 2D Adaptive, 3D Pocket and 3D Finish are); set the setup's part alignment back to As modelled, or machine it in another setup\n```\n\nMaintainer: \"why would i not be able to reorientate my part?! or rotate my WCS's..\"\n\nExpected: each operation kind generates in a setup that holds the part turned. To turn the part or the WCS is a normal step of a job.\n\nEvidence:\n- The guard is `setup_align::generation_problem` in `crates/app/src/setup_align.rs`.\n- PR #2214 (#2210) removed the same guard for area controls. It found that the code already read the picks in the setup frame.\n- #763 (in review) makes one machining-frame seam for part alignment and tilt. Check its PR for overlap first.\n\nWork:\n- List each operation kind that the guard refuses (2D Offset, and the others).\n- For each kind, prove with a test that the generator reads its geometry in the setup frame, then remove the refusal. Use turns about more than one axis, not only 90 degrees about Z.\n- If a kind does not read the setup frame, add the transform. Do not remove its refusal before that.\n- The verify check and the post gate do not change.\n\nSafety: this work changes which programs post. A kind that reads the model frame in a turned setup cuts in the wrong place. Keep the refusal for each kind that has no proof.\n\nDone means: no operation kind refuses a setup only because the part is turned, or each kind that still refuses has its own issue. A test for each kind compares the path in a turned setup with the path of the same part modelled in that position.\n",
